        {
          "kicker": "Ticket sales",
          "heading": "England trail New Zealand and South Africa in Nations Championship sell-outs",
          "body": "The inaugural Nations Championship finals weekend at Twickenham has seen New Zealand and South Africa sell out their dedicated 1,000-ticket allocations. While England fans still account for the bulk of overall sales, the home side's specific quota was increased to 2,000 to meet initial demand. Approximately 60–65% of tickets are now sold for the three-day festival in November. Organisers remain confident despite England's last Twickenham appearance, a 42-21 defeat by Ireland, potentially affecting current individual ticket availability."
