          "kicker": "Selection prospect",
          "heading": "Hector Patterson attracts interest from English clubs ahead of potential switch",
          "body": "Edinburgh scrum-half Hector Patterson is attracting interest from English clubs, including Bath, as he approaches the end of his current contract. While the 21-year-old has represented Scotland at age-grade level, including a win at the 2024 World Rugby U20 Trophy, he remains eligible for England through his grandparents. With the 2027 Rugby World Cup approaching, his next contract decision may influence his senior international future. Patterson is currently an Edinburgh player and no deal has been agreed with any outside club."
